2026-07-13 correction to the PR #475 comment above:

The declaration is **not review-clear and not remotely proven at final head**. Remote Check 29279869383 failed on shallow release-characterization history; 29280783526 passed only old head `66572c3`. Release Proof 29281192288 was canceled before execution when later adversarial review found additional contract defects.

The open amendment now:
- removes per-attempt model demand so every attempt structurally inherits the transition's exact model;
- makes same-route handles inherited and validates alternate account/route inequality;
- freezes carrier auth stripping/injection, fixed-origin/TLS/SSRF rejects, replay reservations, cancellation, typed teardown, bounded waits, and shared leases;
- replaces generic extension objects with typed scalar `x_flag_*` / `x_count_*` / `x_ratio_*` compatibility fields and reserves identity/credential-bearing names;
- adds positive/negative Draft 2020-12 fixtures plus semantic cross-attempt validation;
- keeps the evidence packet explicitly draft.

TIN-1798 remains In Progress. Prompt 78 and Phase 1 remain open until the amended generated schema is current, final-head CI/GF/release/public-source/provenance gates pass, and management surfaces reconcile. No runtime or TIN-2057 golden credit.

2026-07-13 TIN-1798 acceptance item 1 PR opened: [oauth-mux #475](https://github.com/Jesssullivan/oauth-mux/pull/475), head `d43af47`.

Bounded scope:
- Zig-owned managed-harness JSON-RPC surface v2 declaration;
- seven lifecycle methods, all explicitly `not_implemented`;
- method-bound request/result schemas with ordinary additive unknown fields and recursive sensitive-name rejection;
- opaque handles, exact-model demand, max two upstream attempts, and linked `-32099`/`-32601` error responses;
- checked schema generation/drift gate and release declaration consumption while status remains `planned_unshipped`;
- broker surface v1 and live dispatch remain unchanged.

Focused local debugging is green under Zig 0.14.1 for the module tests, full `zig build test`, native build, schema drift, test-root coverage, authority drift, endpoint-free, secrets scan, JSON projection assertions, and diff checks. Two adversarial review rounds found five enforcement defects (invalid null keyword, unbound method/result rules, sensitive-name bypass, unreferenced errors, then nested sensitive-name bypass); all were fixed and final re-review was clear.

Authoritative branch Remote Validate `check` is running as [29279869383](https://github.com/Jesssullivan/oauth-mux/actions/runs/29279869383). PR CI and exact-branch Release Proof also remain merge gates.

Claim boundary: declaration/compatibility artifact only. No adapter round-trip, Claude sidecar, managed launch, account switch, OpenCode conformance, or TIN-2057 golden credit. TIN-1798 remains In Progress after this PR; acceptance items 2-5 remain open.

2026-07-13 Phase-1 declaration slice started from proven main `bb3e5ff` in clean worktree `/private/tmp/omux-tin-1798-schema`, branch `jess/tin-1798-managed-harness-v2-schema-20260713`.

Bounded scope:
- add one Zig-owned `managed-harness-jsonrpc` surface-v2 declaration and deterministic checked schema;
- freeze opaque handle, exact-model, route/lease snapshot, typed transition, repair handoff, teardown, and one-alternate vocabulary;
- mark every method explicitly `not_implemented`;
- preserve shipped broker JSON-RPC surface v1 byte-for-contract and leave `main.zig`, `cli.zig`, broker dispatch, and all adapters untouched;
- wire fail-closed schema drift and forbidden credential/restart/login methods into remote check.

Claim gate: schema declaration only. No listener, sidecar, managed launch, Claude/Codex/OpenCode conformance, or v0.2 runtime claim. TIN-1798 stays open after this slice.

2026-07-31 bounded source-lane claim

Codex seat claims a disjoint Linux containment precursor on branch `codex/tin-2723-linux-service-containment-20260731`:

- systemd-user command runs under an exact `/usr/bin/env -i` allowlist;
- Linux service status becomes fixed-field/value-free and never emits raw `systemctl status` or journal text;
- source-only mutation tests fail on broad environment inheritance and secret sentinels in unit/status output.

Owned files are limited to the systemd template, keepalive service wrapper, and its containment smoke/docs as necessary. This lane does not touch `dist/install.sh`, release manifests/bundles, Lab, runtime environments, credentials, providers, host installs, or services. Transactional service registration/uninstall remains a later slice after this containment floor. R-TIN-1759 remains closed and TIN-2057 remains 0/11.

2026-07-13 live operator-trust dogfood confirms the first three acceptance legs are implemented and useful.

Observed on neo:
- PATH winner `/Users/[host-local user redacted]/.nix-profile/bin/oauth-mux` reports v0.1.15, SHA `96a9b230...`;
- `~/.local/bin/oauth-mux` and `/opt/homebrew/bin/oauth-mux` report v0.1.14, SHA `cc34a06c...`;
- LaunchAgent `dev.xoxd.omux.keepalive` is running `~/.local/bin/oauth-mux` v0.1.14;
- v0.1.15 `doctor --json` reports `path_shadow.shadowed:true` and `resident.stale:{stale:true,sha_mismatch:true,version_older:true}`.

No upgrade/restart was performed during this read-only audit. This is a clean attended dogfood opportunity: install the chosen current binary through one supported lane, restart/verify the LaunchAgent, prove stale=false and healthy ticks, then capture a redacted dated packet.

Remaining completion gate is still the live Linux systemd-user proof (plus the attended remediation packet if we choose to bank it). This ticket is now In Progress, not Todo.

2026-07-13 PR3 started from proven main `c43a529` in clean worktree `/private/tmp/omux-tin-2050-pr3`, branch `jess/tin-2050-workflow-version-authority-20260713`.

Bounded scope:
- remove independent `0.1.13` defaults from Remote Validate, Release Proof, and Registry Dry Run;
- resolve omitted release versions from the checked `build.zig.zon` authority after checkout, while rejecting explicit mismatches;
- stop interpolating operator-supplied version strings directly into shell command text;
- make published deb/rpm QA manual-only with a required explicit published version, removing the misleading PR fallback to v0.1.9;
- add a fail-closed workflow/version contract smoke to the canonical check chain.

Not in this PR: installer/Homebrew rendering migration, publication, signatures/SBOM/provenance, v0.2 member activation, or Bazel/GF REAPI proof.

2026-07-13 PR1 scope correction after two adversarial reviews.

The initial typed resolved-manifest + generic jq query design was rejected and deleted before commit. It duplicated Zig validation, permitted caller-supplied resolution metadata without a trusted materializer, and risked circular consumer self-attestation.

PR1 is now intentionally one-file and one-consumer:
- `flake.nix` reads checked `release-manifest.json` with `builtins.fromJSON`;
- Nix derives release version, package name, primary executable, and the one same-bytes compatibility executable from the declaration;
- `packages.omux` is added while `packages.oauth-mux`, the shim-bearing default, and Home Manager defaults remain compatible;
- focused checks prove both executable names exist and are byte-identical.

Explicitly not claimed by PR1: target-graph consumption, resolved hashes/signatures/SBOM/provenance, publication safety, a generic query API, or migration of any non-Nix consumer. Those remain open under TIN-2050 and must be added only with a concrete materializer/consumer.

